From 62694cac2dc9fc25fda92257961b9dfbff747400 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:38:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the plane samplers leave the rows of the bars out
 too

Where the area outside the active picture is written at the start of the
shader (a picture that is not scaled), the reconstruction is skipped
for those pixels, but the planes were still sampled for them: the chroma
planes and the planes of the enhancement layer are scaled up to 2160
rows in two passes each, the first into a texture of its own. In a
2.39:1 film a quarter of those rows are bars.

libplacebo is now told the rows that hold picture (its patch 9912,
pl_render_params.active_rows), and its plane samplers return at once for
the others, in both passes. What is drawn does not change: no pass reads
a row of the bars for a row of the picture, and the bars get the value
that the early return writes, as before. It is tied to that early
return: without it (a picture that is scaled, the setting that turns it
off, a render that failed with it) nothing is told to libplacebo.

The sampler that is merged into the shader of the target tells the rows
by the coordinates of the target and only compiles where
PL_ACTIVE_ROWS_TARGET is defined, which the hook that writes the bars
now does. If libplacebo drew a plane in a pass of its own, the render
fails and is made again without the early hook, the way a failure of
that hook already is.

Measured on a software OpenGL ES (dvrender_test): every drawing gives
the bytes it gave before, with the bars of the stream, with bars forced
at the sides only, and with different bars on every side. The time it
saves on a GPU is not measured.

The idea is the "active rows" of the Intel Dolby Vision LibreELEC fork
(CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV, R1.0.0 Beta2).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index fa6c4c1..2952cfc 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -59,7 +59,9 @@ static struct pl_hook_res skip_inactive_area(struct active_mask *mask,
         {.var=pl_var_uint("early_count"), .data=&mask->count, .dynamic=true},
         {.var=pl_var_uint("early_flip"), .data=&mask->flip, .dynamic=true}};
     struct pl_custom_shader shader = {
-        .prelude="#define DVBRIDGE_BARS_WRITTEN 1\n", /* see bars_written_in_this_shader() */
+        /* see bars_written_in_this_shader(), and active_rows in render() */
+        .prelude="#define DVBRIDGE_BARS_WRITTEN 1\n"
+                 "#define PL_ACTIVE_ROWS_TARGET 1\n",
         .input=PL_SHADER_SIG_COLOR, .output=PL_SHADER_SIG_COLOR,
         .description="Skip reconstruction outside the DV active picture",
         .variables=vars, .num_variables=packed ? 4 : 1,
@@ -357,6 +359,19 @@ static bool render(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *source,
                       !geometry.x && !geometry.y &&
                       geometry.width == 3840 && geometry.height == 2160 &&
                       (margins[0] || margins[1] || margins[2] || margins[3]);
+    /* Hades: with the bars written first, the samplers of the planes leave their rows out as
+     * well (libplacebo-9912): the chroma planes and the planes of the enhancement layer are
+     * scaled up in two passes each, a quarter of which is rows of the bars in a 2.39:1 film.
+     * The first of those passes draws to a texture of its own, where the early return of
+     * skip_inactive_area() does not reach. Nothing reads those rows: the second pass takes
+     * each row from the same row, and the rows of the bars are written by that return. The
+     * sampler that is part of this shader only compiles where PL_ACTIVE_ROWS_TARGET is
+     * defined, which skip_inactive_area() does: if libplacebo drew a plane in another pass,
+     * the render fails and is made again without any of this (render_bars_first()). */
+    if (mask.early_mask) {
+        params.active_rows[0] = (int)margins[2];
+        params.active_rows[1] = 2160 - (int)margins[3];
+    }
     /* libplacebo disables a hook that failed by its signature: each form has its own. */
     const struct pl_hook hook = {
         .stages = PL_HOOK_OUTPUT | (mask.early_mask ? PL_HOOK_NATIVE : 0),
-- 
2.53.0

